INT. DRIVING SCHOOL - SIMULATOR ROOM - DAY

Four mock cockpits in a row, each facing a flickering screen. Pedals taped with duct tape. A poster: "SIGNAL EARLY. SIGNAL OFTEN."

JUNIPER "JUNE" ABARA, 16, braces, grips the wheel with white knuckles. Next to her, MATEO FUENTES, 17, leans back, one foot on the dash. Behind them, IGNACIO HOLLOWAY, 16, scribbles on his palm. Beside him, GRETA SOLBERG, 17, eats gummy worms and watches the road on his screen instead of her own.

A tinny voice from the simulator: "Merge ahead."

MATEO
Merge, merge, merge.

JUNE
I'm merging.

He tips his chair. She hits the brakes. The screen flashes red.

JUNE (CONT'D)
(whisper)
Mateo.

He grins. She swats him. Behind them, Ignacio snickers.

IGNACIO
Nice, June. Pedestrian down.

GRETA
She hit a mailbox.

IGNACIO
Same thing.

June reboots. Her hands steady. She breathes out, picks the road back up, and cruises. The screen glows green.

She turns to Greta, triumphant. Greta offers a gummy worm. June takes it.

MATEO
My turn.

He throws himself into the seat. Slaps the wheel. Floors it. The screen explodes into a crash.

IGNACIO
Mateo!

MATEO
It's a simulator!

Greta laughs so hard she snorts. Ignacio cracks up. June, red-faced, tries not to, fails.

Then the door opens. They all turn. The instructor's clipboard appears first, then his face, grim.

Four hands go up. Then three come down, pointing at Mateo.

GRETA
School bus. He killed the school bus.
